## Workflow Guidance

### Feature-to-Dev PR Process

**Step 1: Create PR from Feature Branch to Dev**
```bash
# Create PR from feature branch to dev (REQUIRED)
FEATURE_BRANCH=$(git branch --show-current)
REPO_URL=$(git config remote.origin.url | sed 's/.*github\.com[:/]\([^/]*\/[^/.]*\).*/\1/')

echo "🔄 Creating PR from ${FEATURE_BRANCH} to dev branch..."

# Get basic PR info
PR_TITLE=$(echo ${FEATURE_BRANCH} | sed 's/^[^/]*\///' | sed 's/-/ /g' | sed 's/\b\w/\u&/g')
BRANCH_TYPE=$(echo ${FEATURE_BRANCH} | cut -d'/' -f1)

# Simple PR body without complex formatting
PR_BODY="This PR implements ${PR_TITLE,,} from ${FEATURE_BRANCH}.

## Changes Made:
- New functionality implemented
- Tests added and passing
- Ready for preview deployment

## Next Steps:
1. Review code changes
2. Add 'preview' label for deployment
3. Test in preview environment
4. Merge to dev after validation"

# Try GitHub MCP server first, fallback to gh CLI
echo "📋 Attempting to create PR using GitHub MCP server..."
if command -v gh &> /dev/null; then
    echo "🔄 Using GitHub CLI as fallback..."
    gh pr create \
        --base dev \
        --head "${FEATURE_BRANCH}" \
        --title "${BRANCH_TYPE}: ${PR_TITLE}" \
        --body "${PR_BODY}" \
        --draft false
    
    if [ $? -eq 0 ]; then
        echo "✅ PR created successfully with GitHub CLI"
    else
        echo "❌ Failed to create PR with GitHub CLI"
        echo "📋 Opening GitHub PR interface..."
        open "https://github.com/${REPO_URL}/compare/dev...${FEATURE_BRANCH}"
    fi
else
    echo "⚠️  GitHub CLI not available, opening web interface..."
    open "https://github.com/${REPO_URL}/compare/dev...${FEATURE_BRANCH}"
fi
```

